Location: Singapore (Hybrid Work)
Industry: B2C Lead Generation | Digital Marketing

About eGENTIC
At eGENTIC, we help brands grow by connecting them with real people through data-driven lead generation. Operating in over 20 countries, we support some of the world’s biggest names in finance, insurance, and consumer services.


As we continue to expand our presence in Taiwan, we are looking for a commercially driven Sales Manager to develop new client relationships, grow revenue, and strengthen our position in the Taiwan market.


Job Description:
As the Sales Maestro for Taiwan, you'll be the right-hand man in charge of our lead generation ship in the country. We need someone who is not only familiar with Taiwan but has a sales track record that speaks louder than a rock concert.


What We're Hunting For:

- A market maven who crafts sales relationships with direct customers and advertising/media agencies. Get ready to unleash your creativity and whip up business presentations that leave everyone in awe!&nbsp;
- A true hunter mindset who thrives on connecting with people, a prospecting pro who can cold-call like it's nobody's business. You live for bringing in new business. Generate leads independently from scratch and thrive on turning prospects into partners.
- A sales virtuoso with killer communication and negotiation skills. You close deals, manage expectations, and solve problems like a superhero. You're the architect of country plans that scream sales growth.&nbsp;
- An Individual contributor who takes ownership and can work independently. Identify key prospects, build a strategic sales approach, and let's talk about taking the world by storm!&nbsp;Ideal for someone who passionate about achieving sales goals, 
- A team player who dances seamlessly with every function in the company, contributing to the success of the country team, supporting your team to greatness.&nbsp;


Candidates with more experience in sales may be considered for a senior position.


Qualifications:

- A passion for navigating through Taiwan and embracing its dynamic market landscape.
- Proficiency in the native language of the region to effectively interact with clients and business partners. 
- A rock-solid background in sales and business development, with a history of hitting targets out of the park.&nbsp;
- Leadership skills that could rival a rock band manager. Team building and development are your jam.&nbsp;
- The ability to think strategically and execute plans like a chess grandmaster.&nbsp;
- Communication and interpersonal skills that could charm the socks off anyone.&nbsp;
- Analytical and problem-solving abilities sharper than a ninja's sword.&nbsp;
- Bonus points if you've rocked the lead generation or digital marketing scene.&nbsp;
- Willingness to travel extensively for the role, ensuring hands-on engagement with clients and markets.
- A degree in marketing, business, or a related field – because we like our team educated and ready to rock!&nbsp;


What We Offer:

- A salary that'll make your bank account do a happy dance, plus performance-based bonuses.&nbsp;
- Uncapped Commissions
- Opportunities to spread your wings and grow professionally.
- The chance to be a big shot in our North/Northeast Asia expansion.
- A supportive and collaborative work environment
- A flexible work culture because we know you're a rockstar on and off the stage.&nbsp;


If you're a motivated, results-driven professional with a knack for the Taiwan market and a passion for sales, we want you! 


Join eGENTIC and be part of an exciting journey delivering top-tier consumer leads to businesses in these regions. This opportunity is based in the heart of Singapore – let's create some excitement together! 🚀&nbsp;

Job Purpose:
Partner Account Manager (PAM) represents Kaspersky Lab to the Channel, communicates the strategy and vision. For Kaspersky Lab Partners, PAM serves as main point of entry for any business-related questions, and advocates the partner within Kaspersky Lab.


This role is partner-facing with the core accountability of landing renewal sales through Managed Partners portfolio, develops New Business and recruits new Managed Partners.


Main responsibilities:
Partners Relationships Management
• Work with assigned portfolio of Managed partners to ensure revenue targets are met;
• Partners Joint Business planning and plan execution, maintain established Rhythm of Business (QBR, MBR, and others);
• Serve as main point of entry for any business-related questions and needs, be a trusted adviser for all levels and roles in Partner;
• Align partners strategy with region sales and development strategy;
• Perform Partners management in a compliant way, follow the channel rules of engagement, make sure Partners comply with Kaspersky Lab business policies;
• Help to connect Kaspersky Lab partner community and Kaspersky Lab Area level to drive partner satisfaction;
• Advocate the partner within Kaspersky Lab;


Partners Performance Management 
• Drive New Business development and find New Managed Partners to work with;
• Maintain renewals rate target;
• Execute on Partners Enablement and Growth engines;
• Drive upsell/cross-sell opportunities in assigned Managed Partners portfolio;
• Participate in trainings and readiness sessions to be able to pitch to Managed Partners new products, product features, licensing, sales skills, partner program and other KL programs;
• Makes Managed Partners utilize every Partner program feature: Deal Registrations, Incentives, Rebates, Leads transfer, etc.;
• Review SMB and mid-market customer opportunities and use all available resources to accelerate deal closure;
• Manage Partners participation in KL marketing programs and help to land marketing activities, collaborates with Regional Marketing department;


Enterprise Partners Management 
• Work with assigned Enterprise &amp; SI Partners to ensure Enterprise revenue targets are met
• Orchestrated internal resources within Enterprise Team
• Manage and review pipeline of Enterprise partners
• Drives Account planning process


Qualification Requirements
• Minimum 7-10 years of sales experience, preferably in cybersecurity industry, including at least 5 years of experience in partner or channel management;
• Proven track record of achievement against quota;
• Reasonable level of technical proficiency;
• Inclusive and collaborative – driving teamwork and cross-team alignment;
• Strong partner relationship management;
• Strong executive presence including communication and presentation skills with a high degree of comfort to large and small audiences;
• Bachelor’s degree required;
• Experience in working with Security solutions is an advantage;
• SFDC knowledge preferred.

The Senior Conference Producer / Senior Conference Marketing Specialist is a full-time position based in Singapore. As a Senior Conference Producer / Senior Conference Marketing Specialist, you will play a key role as the driving force behind academic conferences. You will gain hands-on experience in all aspects of conference management from concept to execution, with specific responsibilities depending on the type of event. You can let us know your preference during the interview for Senior Conference Producer or Senior Conference Marketing Specialist role.

For virtual conferences, you will be responsible for overseeing both the production and marketing aspects, ensuring seamless execution and maximum engagement throughout the event.

For in-person conferences, you will be responsible for either production or marketing, though your role may extend beyond these areas as additional tasks arise, depending on the needs of the event.

You will be responsible for the following areas:

Production



- Market Research: Conduct in-depth research on market trends, competitor landscapes, and industry challenges; 
- Value proposition Creation: Discuss valid topics with the chair and write and delivering event briefs for the marketing and editorial teams; 
- Conference agenda curation: Coordinate with chair and session chairs to select the oral and poster presentation candidates, schedule the presentation timing for all slots; 
- Stakeholder Engagement: Establish relationships with key stakeholders, including chair, session chairs, speakers to create advocacy for our events; 
- Website Management: Keep event websites updated with the latest information, speakers, partners, and sessions; 
- Budget Preparation and Tracking: Prepare budget forecast before the event, and update the budget regularly to check the potential profit and loss; 
- Customer Service: Provide exceptional service to partners, speakers, and stakeholders, resolving issues promptly; 
- Milestone Tracking: Monitor and track progress to ensure KPIs and event targets are achieved; 
- Team Coordination: Coordinate with editorial team, marketing team, live session teams; 
- Editorial progress monitor: Work closely with the editorial team on abstract processing and with production teams on abstract book preparation; 
- Oversee live streaming of virtual events to ensure the smooth operation of the live sessions; 
- Onsite Delivery: Lead the creation and delivery of event briefs for on-site delivery, ensuring exceptional on-site execution of the conferences to meet customer expectations;

Marketing



- Marketing strategy creation: Ensure maximum outreach to target markets and promote the conference through various channels 
- Conference collateral materials creation: draft copies for brochures, banners, sponsorship prospectus
- Marketing Copywriting: Create promotional copy for marketing channels, including Email campaigns, SM posts, Media partners and editorial needs. 
- SEO marketing: Improve the website ranking and increase the website traffic; 
- Sponsorship marketing: Secure partners and coordinate their participation and sponsorship; 
- Content Development: Create content for conference sessions, interviews, and speaker/host scripts by collaborating with internal and external stakeholders; 
- Marketing campaigns progress tracking: Monitor and track progress to ensure the timely execution of all marketing schedules; 
- Post-Event Analysis: Conduct evaluations and prepare detailed reports highlighting event outcomes.

Others



- Recognize work processes and/or outcomes that are negatively impacting the project; owns the issue and takes action to address deficiencies by identifying resolutions and notifying the appropriate manager.

Requirements:



- A Bachelor or Master's degree in any subject;
- Candidates with at least 2 years of relevant experience are welcome to apply
- Experience in conference industry is preferred
- Are curious about people and love to speak, build and nurture relations;
- Capable of handling multiple projects, and articulate common objectives for the teams to follow.
- Excellent online call etiquette and written communication skills
- International travel and confidence in face-to-face networking
- Proven ability to work well in a team but also initiative to work on your own

What We Offer:



- Professional and personal development
- International work environment
- Flexible working hours in the limits of a full-time job
- Trips to the other MDPI offices
- Attending Scientific Conferences
- Competitive salary, benefits

A pioneer in scholarly open access publishing, MDPI has supported academic communities since 1996. Our mission is to foster open scientific exchange in all forms, across all disciplines. We operate more than 400 diverse, peer-reviewed, open access journals supported by over 66,000 academic editors. We serve scholars from around the world to ensure the latest research is openly and broadly available.

MDPI is headquartered in Switzerland with additional offices in Europe, Asia and North America. We are committed to ensuring that high quality research is made available as quickly as possible. We also support sustainability projects, with sustainability as a key theme in many journals and through the MDPI Sustainability Foundation.

Company Description

foodpanda is part of the Delivery Hero Group, the world’s pioneering local delivery platform, our mission is to deliver an amazing experience—fast, easy, and to your door. We operate in around 65 countries worldwide. Headquartered in Berlin, Germany. Delivery Hero has been listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange since 2017 and is part of the MDAX stock market index.

Job Description

As the leader of our Local Shops vertical, you will own the end-to-end business across our three brands (foodpanda, foodora and yemeksepeti) spanning Asia, Europe and Turkey. Local Shops is our partner-powered quick commerce business, where we bring the assortment of the region’s leading retailers to customers in minutes. You will set the strategy, own the commercial agenda with our retail partners, and be accountable for the operational quality that turns a partnership into a great customer experience. You will lead a regional team across commercial and operations, and work hand in hand with country teams to grow the vertical aggressively.

Key Responsibilities:

Own the vertical strategy and roadmap: define where we play (grocery today; health & beauty, DIY, pet and further verticals next), how we win, and the KPI framework and portfolio of initiatives to get there;

Be accountable for the growth and unit economics of the vertical, steering performance through clear business reviews and disciplined prioritisation of resources;

Develop and own senior relationships with our regional strategic retail partners: shaping joint business plans, commercial terms, assortment, pricing and monetisation;

Guide country commercial teams in their sales agenda, account management, category management and monetisation topics, raising the bar on execution across all markets;

Own operational excellence end to end: partner store execution (availability, picking quality, substitutions, stock accuracy), handover to riders, delivery performance, and the customer experience metrics that follow;

Build the playbooks, tooling requirements and best practices that let every country execute consistently, acting as the bridge between regional strategy and local reality;

Lead, structure and develop a regional team spanning commercial and operations, fostering collaboration, learning and high performance;

Work cross-functionally with product, data, logistics, marketing and finance to co-create the solutions the vertical needs to scale;

Provide senior management with regular updates on vertical performance, partner developments and market insights.

Qualifications

10+ years of professional experience, with at least 3–5 years leading a business unit, vertical or P&L in a senior role;
Leadership experience across both commercial and operational teams, including direct management of managers and key accounts;
Strong strategic thinking and project leadership skills, with the ability to translate frameworks into impactful local execution;
Experience in B2B account management or joint business planning with large retailers or marketplaces;
Proven track record of driving operational performance in a retail, e-commerce, logistics or on-demand environment;
Excellent stakeholder management skills across different cultures, levels and functions;
Highly analytical, data-driven, and comfortable making decisions based on insights;
Hands-on mentality with the ability to operate both at strategic and operational levels;
Outstanding communication and negotiation skills, with fluent English (other regional languages are a plus);
Willingness to travel across the region as needed;
Nice to Have:
Background in retail operations, supply chain or last-mile logistics;
Previous exposure to management consulting, strategic project management, or business development roles;
Familiarity with CRM tools (e.g. Salesforce) and data analytics platforms.

