Job Description

The Director User Retention will lead user growth and engagement strategies across 16 countries and three brands, focusing on expanding and retaining our active user base. This role is key to developing our new verticals offerings to drive user retention and increased engagement. You will lead a team of 15+ managers and individual contributors, all dedicated to optimizing and growing our user ecosystem effectively.

Main responsibilities:



- Own User Retention and Engagement: You set the strategic direction for the retention and New verticals team and drive initiatives to support the positive development of the key user retention and engagement metrics across our offerings; 
- Optimize Retention ROI: Continuously refine user lifecycle communications and investments, encouraging users to adopt and retain high-value behaviours through communication triggers, discounts, and coupons at always-improving ROIs; 
- Accelerate New Vertical Adoption: Collaborate with Quick Commerce business counterparts to set the strategy for accelerating Quick Commerce adoption and retention. You will drive the efficient and effective use of the Quick Commerce vertical’s marketing budget: 
- Enhance Segmentation, Targeting, and Experimentation: Continuously improve user segmentation, enhance targeting, and lead the design and execution of experiments to boost customer retention and engagement, working closely with Product and data teams to support your objectives; 
- Drive Cross-Functional Collaboration and Alignment: Partner effectively with Product, Data, Marketing, and our local + central teams to pressure-test our retention strategy and deliver on the right growth initiatives. 

Qualifications



- Minimum 12 years in relevant fields, with 5+ years in B2C tech (growth or marketing) and roles like management consulting, investment banking, or strategy in high-growth environments; Quick Commerce experience in customer adoption/retention is a plus;
- Proven ability to lead large teams (10+ people) and foster professional growth at all levels;
- Strong interpersonal skills with a track record of influencing senior leadership and aligning cross-functional teams;
- Skilled in data-driven decision-making and comfortable working in ambiguous, dynamic market conditions;
- Familiarity with CRM and marketing automation tools, such as Braze or HubSpot, is a plus.

The Chinese Media Group (CMG) is seeking a highly motivated Performance Marketing &amp; Campaign Specialist to join its Branding & Marketing (B&M) team. The B&M section is responsible for co-developing and implementing respective CMG’s products brands strategies, as well as driving effective marketing and communication plans to create strong brand value; these include Lianhe Zaobao, Shin Min Daily News, ThinkChina, ZBSchools, HeyKaki, UFM100.3 and 96.3 Hao FM etc.


As a Performance Marketing &amp; Campaign Specialist, you will be the subject matter expert in omnichannel marketing efforts, especially in driving digital performances, generating brand awareness and engagement, in not only Singapore, but also Asia and global regions. You are expected to:



- Develop a thorough understanding of CMG and its brands’ mission and business goals;
- Set up campaigns, optimize audience targeting, ad placement and ROI across programmatic, display, social media, SEM, email marketing etc. to increase effectiveness of ads;
- Coordinate closely with internal stakeholders such as branding specialists, regional marketer, lifecycle marketer, designer, social media, ad operations etc. to execute marketing plans of varying scales within budget;
- Research and develop top to mid marketing funnel strategy for CMG brands, using paid digital marketing to amplify and effectively increase market share;
- Derive benchmarks and KPIs, monitor, analyze and report campaign performance to internal and external stakeholders, where applicable;
- Utilize data and insights to recommend opportunities for improvement and guide strategic decisions;
- Support with copywriting and creation of various communication materials, primarily campaign artworks for owned platforms and social media etc.;
- Liaise with internal and external stakeholders for approval of key artwork, communication materials;
- Research and provide industry updates, trends and insights that can help create potential opportunities;
- Provide guidance to internal stakeholders on digital campaign optimization;
- Build and manage relationships with vendors, ad platform partners, and agencies;
- Perform knowledge sharing within the B&amp;M team, as well as within CMG to educate and inform on best practices; and
- Ensure confidentiality of all channel and performance data.


Job Requirements

- Degree/Diploma holder with at least 3 years of related working experience in media, digital marketing or agency;
- Proven experience in developing and executing media placement across various channels (e.g. Google, Meta, TikTok, X, Taboola, Outbrain, Baidu, WeChat etc.) in Singapore and global regions;
- Proven experience in using marketing analytics tools and data visualization tools, including but not limited to GA4, Lookerstudio, Tableau, Excel, Google Sheets etc;
- Proven experience in ad platforms integration with strong working knowledge in API, SDK or event creating on GTM;
- Strong working knowledge of the digital media space with an emphasis in paid social, search, display, video and mobile etc;
- Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English and Mandarin, as this role mainly supports Chinese products;
- Able to produce effective presentations, and appreciate compelling content;
- Kept abreast of changes in marketing and content trends, technologies, social media landscape and consumer behaviors;
- Highly proactive, detail-oriented and good at project management; good news sense would be advantageous;
- Able to multitask with tight deadlines in a fast-paced environment;
- Able to work independently but also connect with people and collaborate as a team; and
- Able to work on weekends due to campaigns.

Job Description

- Responsible for the payment business growth of Indonesia/Vietnam as a tourist destination under Alipay+ payment gateway (where the main KPI will be number of active payment users, daily average transactions, total payment value, revenue)
- Develop growth strategies based on in-depth research on inbound travel market trends, competitor dynamics, and user needs for tourists coming to Indonesia/Vietnam from mainland China and around the world, and in collaboration with various stakeholders including marketing and growth teams from the headquarter and Alipay+ mobile payment partners, key industry merchants/suppliers, tourism board, government and intellectual property (IP) partners.
- Design, execute and evaluate integrated marketing campaigns across online/offline channels and within/outside the app (including user acquisition, activation, retention, and major promotions) to strengthen user awareness of Alipay+ payment availability and deals, so as to drive business growth.
- Collaborate with business development team to identify and manage key merchant accounts across different categories (F&amp;B, attractions, retail, etc.) in the market, in order to win trust, establish joint marketing partnerships and drive their publicity and payment volume.
- Other ad-hoc duties as assigned.


Requirements

- Bachelor's degree or higher, major preferably in Business or Marketing;
- At least 3 years experience in marketing and growth operations in a consumer facing internet/fintech industry; Candidates with background in online-to-offline (O2O) business, payment business or travel industry, along with proven success cases in driving business growth, are preferred.
- Must have: Proficiency in both English and Mandarin. Excellence in Chinese content copy-writing.
- Must have: Familiar with mainland China market internet landscape and user behavior. Familiar with Chinese social media environment and marketing dynamics;
- Possess big picture thinking and strong data acumen, while ready to get hands-on;
- Flexible team player who thrives in fast-paced, often ambiguous, environment;
- Curious, optimistic, resilient, highly adaptable, and able to work effectively under pressure;
- Ability to set priorities, problem solve, multi-task and work independently;
- Excellent communication skills with a proven track record of cross-functional and cross-team collaboration. Able to efficiently gather information, build consensus, and drive project execution;
- Excellent Excel and PowerPoint capabilities; experience in enhancing productivity through AI is a plus.

