Key Responsibilities

Strategy & Business Development

Develop and execute the institutional channel strategy, expanding partnerships with banks, card schemes (Visa/Mastercard), acquirers, clearing and settlement networks, remittance and stablecoin providers;

Identify and enter new channels and markets (Southeast Asia, APAC and beyond), driving channel coverage and scaled growth across multi-currency acquiring, issuing and collection.

Commercial Negotiation & Onboarding

Lead commercial negotiations of institutional agreements (pricing, settlement cycles, security deposits, service levels), driving signing and implementation;

Manage the full channel onboarding lifecycle (KYB, technical integration, testing and go-live), ensuring partnerships meet the company's compliance and risk requirements.

Channel Product & Routing

Partner with Product and Engineering to optimise transaction routing, success rates and settlement efficiency, productising channel capabilities for reuse;

Monitor channel stability and cost structure, continuously optimising unit transaction cost and capital efficiency.

Channel Operations & Relationship Management

Establish channel operations mechanisms (reconciliation, discrepancy handling, chargeback/dispute coordination) to ensure transaction continuity and merchant experience;

Maintain senior-level relationships with institutional partners, organising regular business reviews and joint growth plans.

Compliance & Regulatory Alignment

Work with Compliance and Risk to ensure channel partnerships meet the MAS Payment Services Act and AML/KYC, sanctions screening and other regulatory requirements;

Support licence applications, maintenance and regulatory inspections with channel-related compliance materials and evidence.

Market Intelligence & Industry Network

Track trends in cross-border payments, card scheme rules, clearing networks, stablecoins and Web3 payments, providing channel strategy recommendations;

Represent the company in industry events and ecosystem initiatives, raising its influence across the institutional landscape.

Team Leadership

Build and lead the institutional channels team from scratch, establishing goals, processes and performance mechanisms;

Coordinate collaboration across Singapore, Hong Kong and Shenzhen to build a specialised regional channel capability centre.

Requirements

Basic Qualifications

Bachelor's degree or above in Finance, Economics, International Trade, Business Management or related disciplines;

8+ years of institutional channels / business development experience in cross-border payments, banking, acquiring or fintech, including 3+ years of team management (outstanding candidates may be considered with 5+ years of relevant experience and 2+ years of management);

Hands-on experience in channel partnerships with licensed payment institutions, banks or card schemes.

Professional Skills

Solid knowledge of acquiring, cross-border collection/remittance and issuing flows, familiar with Visa/Mastercard scheme rules and clearing and settlement systems (SWIFT, local clearing, FAST/PayNow, etc.);

Strong institutional-level commercial negotiation and contract management skills, able to independently drive direct bank connections and channel onboarding;

Understanding of FX, settlement cycles and funding cost structuring and optimisation;

Familiarity with stablecoin settlement and Web3 payment channels is preferred.

Compliance & Governance

Knowledge of Singapore MAS payment regulations and AML/KYC, sanctions screening requirements;

Experience in payment licence applications, maintenance or regulatory engagement is preferred.

Language & Soft Skills

Fluent in English as the working language (Singapore office working language); proficiency in Chinese is a plus (for collaboration with China HQ, Hong Kong and Shenzhen teams);

Excellent cross-cultural communication and senior stakeholder management, comfortable in a fast-paced, multi-market environment;

Results-driven, with an entrepreneurial mindset to build from zero to one.

